{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap and return rules (AB 12)","requirement":"Most landlords may charge only one month's rent as a security deposit; small owners of no more than two rental properties with four units total may charge two months. The deposit must be returned with an itemized statement within 21 days.","key_value":"1 month's rent; up to 2 months' rent for owners of 2 rental properties with 4 units total","coverage_conditions":"Applies to security deposits for residential tenancies in California. Most landlords may charge only one month's rent; owners of no more than two rental properties with four units total may charge two months.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"landlord who owns only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC all of whose members are natural persons","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Photo documentation applies to tenancies beginning on or after July 1, 2025; the cleaning deduction applies to tenancies beginning after January 1, 2003; last month's rent is part of the deposit, first month's rent is not.","coverage_quotes":["Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","Starting July 1, 2024, landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total can charge up to two months' rent for furnished and unfurnished units if ownership is held by a natural person, family trust, or limited liability company (LLC) where all members are natural persons"]},"exemptions":"Landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, if held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons, may charge up to two months' rent.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"AB 12","quoted_span":"Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance security deposit interest","requirement":"Landlords of units covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year, and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"other","text":"units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance"}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
